    "Agents told to \"streamline\" optimise for length, because length is the thing they can see. The no-op test is behavioural, not aesthetic: delete the line and ask whether the agent's behaviour changed. When a sentence fails, delete the whole sentence rather than trim words from it — and settle a disagreement about it by running the document, not by arguing.": "被要求「精简」的智能体会为长度而优化，因为长度是它们看得见的东西。无操作测试是行为层面的，不是审美层面的：删掉那一行，问智能体的行为是否变了。当一个句子不合格时，删除整个句子而不是删减其中的词——关于它的分歧，用运行文档来裁决，而不是争论。",
    "aggressively: the whole reason the route stays current is that uncertainty is flushed out by cheap concrete artifacts before implementation depends on it. Wayfinder is \"prototypemaxxing\", not \"planmaxxing\".": "激进地：这条路线保持当下的全部原因，就是不确定性在实现依赖它之前，就被便宜的具象产物冲刷掉了。Wayfinder 是「原型拉满」，不是「规划拉满」。",
