    "outputs assume a single person curating them. A two-developer team running four months in one repo reported state drift on roughly 20% of sampled merged PRs, with ADR citations and README claims the highest-drift surfaces — deliberate, human-curated docs drifted worse than agent memory did. Pruning the stale docs did not hold; the same sweep was stale again within days. What worked was deleting shadow state outright and adding a deterministic citation and link linter to CI.": "输出假设由一个人策展。一个两人团队在同一个仓库运行四个月后报告，抽样合并 PR 中约 20% 存在状态漂移，ADR 引用和 README 声明是漂移最严重的表面——经过精心人工策展的文档漂移得比智能体记忆更糟。清理过期文档没有持久效果；同样的扫描几天内又过时了。真正有效的是彻底删除影子状态，并给 CI 添加确定性的引用和链接 linter。",
